-- title:
--   Elements fixing Φ pointwise lie in ±Γ₁(M)
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $M$, a field $K$ equipped with a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra structure, an element $t\in K$, and a group homomorphism $\sigma\colon \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})\to \mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{C}}(K)$ whose kernel is the subgroup generated by $\Gamma(M)$ together with $-1$; assume $K$ is finite-dimensional and Galois over the subfield $\mathbb{C}\langle t\rangle$ generated by $t$, of degree equal to the index of $\Gamma(M)\cdot\langle -1\rangle$ in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. Let $\iota\colon \overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to\mathbb{C}$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $F$ denote the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the coefficientwise images of the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ by the quotients of integral $q$-expansions of pairs of modular forms of equal weight on $\Gamma_1(M)$ (denominator nonzero). Let $\Phi\colon F\to K$ be a ring homomorphism and $E'\colon K\to\mathbb{C}((q))$ a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra homomorphism with $E'(t)$ the series $q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3\eta^{-24}$-type integral expansion$)$ of $j$ with $q$ replaced by $q^M$, and $E'(\Phi u)$ equal to the $q\mapsto q^M$ substitution applied to the $\iota$-image of $u$ for every $u\in F$. Assume further that $\Phi$ sends the element $y_0\in F$ whose Laurent series is the $j$-expansion over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to $t$, and that $\sigma(\gamma)$ fixes $\Phi u$ for all $\gamma\in\Gamma_1(M)$ and all $u$. Then any $\delta\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ with $\sigma(\delta)(\Phi u)=\Phi u$ for all $u$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\Gamma_1(M)$ and $-1$.
--
--   This is the Galois-correspondence step identifying the pointwise fixer of the image of the function field of $X_1(M)$ inside $\mathrm{Gal}(K/\mathbb{C}(t))$ as exactly $\pm\Gamma_1(M)/\pm\Gamma(M)$, the inclusion in the nontrivial direction. It is used in the descent computation of ramification orders for the $\Gamma_1(M)$ base change over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, via the degree formula $[\,\mathbb{C}\cdot F : \mathbb{C}(j(q^M))\,]=[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}):\pm\Gamma_1(M)]$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_LevelN_Descent_fixer_le.lean

